# The build context is an allowlist: everything is left out, then the code
# and the files it finds beside the package are let back in. A checkout is
# often also a live root (cousins/, config/ with keys, .secrets/, run/,
# data/, shared/, secrets/ for the compose secret); a denylist leaks the
# next secret-bearing path the framework learns to write, an allowlist
# cannot. Left out with everything else: .git, tests, docs, examples (a
# rendered home for tests/test_examples.py; nothing in cousin_lib reads it),
# systemd (bare-host units), CI and compose files.
*
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!cousin_lib
!templates
!hooks
!plugins
!config/*.example
!docker/entrypoint.sh
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
